  "description": "Restic uses native Rabin around 1 MiB, explicit Zstd auto, 8 MiB pack targets and mandatory encryption. Gutch uses a nominal 1 MiB FastCDC target, Zstd 3, 8 MiB compressed bundles and AES-256-GCM repository encryption. Both encrypt, with different schemes. Zstd auto is not an exact level-3 match; bounds, codec implementations and compression units differ. Restore retains --verify; recovery verifies existing bytes and deletes extra files. Fresh repositories and isolated caches. Four workers where exposed; native Borg/BPT scheduling. One warm-up and 6 rotating measured repetitions; profiling off. Measurement contract 2 separates content repair, preserved-mtime damage, extra-file cleanup and full restoration. Strict source-derived SHA-256 validation follows every supported operation; both native and validation-inclusive durations are reported. Unsupported operations receive no timing.",
